238	System One is TypeSafe's model for building AI-powered software, not agents. It does not generate code or choose its own next action. It provides AI primitives that embed into software, so code remains in control while the model handles common-sense judgments over unstructured data.
239	
240	<Info>
241	  **Summary:** build a normal software workflow and insert System One only where AI is needed.
242	
243	  * Keep control flow, deterministic rules, and side effects in code.
244	  * Break broad judgments into narrow, typed questions with explicit instructions and criteria.
245	  * Give each question only the context it needs.
246	  * Use probabilities and confidence to act, ask for review, or escalate.
247	  * Ask independent questions together, then compose their answers in code.
248	</Info>
249	
250	## Three software architectures
251	
252	TypeSafe is designed for building **AI-powered software**, where code owns the workflow and AI handles narrow, structured decisions.
253	
254	<Tabs>
255	  <Tab title="Traditional software">
256	    Traditional code is a complex decision tree made from simple software primitives. Because each primitive is reliable, developers can compose them into higher-level abstractions.
257	  </Tab>
258	
259	  <Tab title="LLM agents">
260	    An agent processes instructions and chooses its next step. This works well when a person is monitoring the process, but every loop introduces another opportunity to go off the rails.
261	  </Tab>
262	
263	  <Tab title="AI-powered software">
264	    Code handles deterministic work and owns the control flow. The model appears only where the system needs programmable common sense or needs to interpret unstructured data. Each AI task is kept atomic and constrained.
265	  </Tab>
266	</Tabs>
267	
268	<Frame>
269	  <img className="block dark:hidden" src="https://mintcdn.com/ts-docs/aFVnpmCIX68NpsV1/images/how-to-build-with-typesafe/software-architectures-light.webp?fit=max&auto=format&n=aFVnpmCIX68NpsV1&q=85&s=35c7622176190d1b1f19dc712f2fbf11" alt="Traditional software, agents, and AI-powered software shown as three different system architectures." width="2048" height="1117" data-path="images/how-to-build-with-typesafe/software-architectures-light.webp" />
